{
  "id": "042",
  "title": "The Tea Master",
  "subtitle": "\"The immortal heavens offered me ascension. I declined. I opened a teahouse on the road between the Five Sects. My customers included demons, elders, and one very persistent Heavenly Emperor.\"",
  "penName": "Feng Qi",
  "genre": "cultivationXianxia",
  "hook": "I reached the Nascent Soul stage at thirty-one. I declined ascension. The immortal heavens were, frankly, exhausting. I built a teahouse on the pilgrimage road between the Five Sects, six days from the nearest city. My sign said *Feng's Humble Cup.* My first customer was a demon on the run. My second was a sect elder in disguise. My third was a widowed swordsman who had stopped looking for vengeance and started looking for peace. I poured tea. I listened. I refused to fight anyone. My cultivation improved anyway.",
